      "train_position": 189,
      "train_qid": "25003",
      "hint": "Extremal \"how long / how many at most\" problems need two halves: an upper bound and a matching construction. State both targets before computing. For bounds, express the required pattern as one closed form in the index (an arithmetic progression is A+B*index), subtract it from each candidate function, and count zeros: a degree-d polynomial minus an affine function is still degree d and not identically zero, so it can match at most d indices. When several functions are available, each contributes its own cap, so add the caps over all functions - do not stop at one function's cap, and do not use the function count alone. Do not chase consecutive differences; that only limits reuse of a single function. Then realize the bound by cutting the index range into consecutive blocks and interpolating one function per block. Commit to this route early instead of enumerating cases.",
